This repository is open source, under different licenses for different
kinds of work. All of them are reciprocal ("copyleft"): you may use, change
and share this work, and changes you share must stay open under the same
terms. Full license texts are in the LICENSES/ folder. Most source files
also name their license on an SPDX-License-Identifier line at the top.

  Arduino libraries - RV112FF/, RA6M5CapTouch/, MultiTurnKnob/,
  RA6M5AnalogTuning/, RA6M5FastSD/ (including their examples):
      GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later (LGPL-3.0-or-later).
      A sketch that just uses one of these libraries can be under any
      license; changes to a library itself must be shared under the LGPL.
      Each library folder carries its own copy (COPYING.LESSER, plus the
      GPL it builds on in COPYING), so it can be split out on its own.

  Everything else that is software - the demo sketches, tools/, pcb/tools/,
  the web pages and the Makefile:
      GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).

  Hardware designs - the KiCad carrier board in pcb/ and the knob model in
  hardware/:
      CERN Open Hardware Licence v2, Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S-2.0).

  Documentation - the .md files, and the tutorial to come:
      Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
      (CC-BY-SA-4.0).

Third-party material, under its own terms:

  - AudioKnobsDemo/faust_support.h and AudioKnobsWebBLEDemo/faust_support.h
    are trimmed copies of the Faust C++ architecture headers, (C) GRAME,
    Centre National de Creation Musicale, under the Faust architecture-file
    license (LGPL with a static-linking exception). See https://faust.grame.fr.

  - synth.h in those folders is generated by the Faust compiler from
    synth.dsp and the Faust standard libraries. The libraries' license
    exception lets compiled output take any license; it is distributed
    under synth.dsp's GPL-3.0-or-later.

  - The board's Thing Plus footprint is derived from pad coordinates in
    SparkFun's KiCad libraries, (C) SparkFun Electronics, CC BY 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
